{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And you shall remember that you were a slave in Egypt</b>: Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Deuteronomy 16:12) says that this is joined with 'and your male slave and your female slave.' But the correct interpretation is according to its plain sense, that you shall observe these statutes that the Master who redeemed you from the house of slaves has commanded you. And so we mention in the sanctification of the day, 'a remembrance of the Exodus from Egypt.' And it says 'these statutes' regarding the Festival of Weeks, because the Torah did not specify the reason for the count of seven weeks and the count of fifty days, and it alone is Atzeret, and I have already mentioned its secret (Leviticus 23:15):"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase וְאָמַר הַחֻקִּים הָאֵלֶּה is rendered as 'it says these statutes,' referring to Scripture's use of the term in this passage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:50:31.067489147Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}